cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Meta-Ethnography Canvas in your research or protocol, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Meta-Ethnography Canvas: An open-source workspace for meta-ethnography, with reporting outputs structured around eMERGe"
version: "1.1.0"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24200375
abstract: "A zero-backend, single-window browser workspace for conducting Meta-Ethnography qualitative evidence synthesis (QES), designed around the eMERGe reporting guideline (France et al., 2019). Supports full-text PDF annotation, 1st/2nd/3rd order construct translation matrices, GRADE-CERQual assessment, reflexive audit trails, and publication-ready Word (.docx) table export."
authors:
  - family-names: "Jeong"
    given-names: "Dae Yun"
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0004-0432-4675
repository-code: "https://github.com/jdaeyun/meta-ethnography-canvas"
url: "https://jdaeyun.github.io/meta-ethnography-canvas/"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-11-13"
keywords:
  - meta-ethnography
  - qualitative-evidence-synthesis
  - systematic-review
  - eMERGe
  - GRADE-CERQual
  - qualitative-research
